{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
Down by the [D]salley [G]gardens
My [D]love and I did [A]meet;
She passed the [D]salley [G]gardens
With [D]little [A]snow-white [D]feet.
She [G]bid me take love [D]easy,
As the [Bm]leaves grow [Em]on the [A]tree;
But [D]I, being young and [G]foolish,
With [D]her would [A]not a[D]gree.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
In a field [D]by the [G]river
My [D]love and I did [A]stand,
And on my [D]leaning [G]shoulder
She [D]laid her [A]snow-white [D]hand.
She [G]bid me take life [D]easy,
As the [Bm]grass grows [Em]on the [A]weirs;
But [D]I was young and [G]foolish,
And [D]now am [A]full of [D]tears.
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: D}
